$ zsh -c 'source scripts/app-nav/uinav.sh && ui_tap "Order status, Delivered" --first'   # after navigating back to the identical screen state
tap 'Order status, Delivered' @ 672 2685
exit=0

-> IDENTICAL coordinates, IDENTICAL exit code between zsh-direct-source and bash -c. Fix confirmed live.

=== Differential proof the mechanism is real (mechanism check, not touching the fixed file) ===
Reproduced the PRE-FIX unquoted-string pattern inline under zsh:
$ zsh -c '
UIFIND="scripts/app-nav/uifind.py"; flags=""
for a in --exact; do case "$a" in --*) flags="$flags $a";; esac; done
ANDROID_SERIAL=emulator-5554 python3 "$UIFIND" find "Order status, Delivered" $flags
'
usage: uifind.py find "<label>" [--exact] [--first]
exit=2
-> Confirms: the OLD string+unquoted-expansion pattern DOES mangle under zsh (usage-line
   fallback, exit 2 instead of AMBIGUOUS exit 3). The fixed array-based code (flags=(),
   "${flags[@]}") above does not exhibit this — proving the fix actually addresses the
   defect, not a vacuous pass.

